   "stem": {
      "text": "The graphs of the functions u and v shown each consist of three line segments on \\( 0 \\le x \\le 6 \\). Let \\( h(x) = u(v(x)) \\). Find the exact value of \\( h'(5) \\).",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         9,
         2
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "By the chain rule, \\( h'(5) = u'(v(5)) \\cdot v'(5) \\). From the graph, \\( v(5) = 3 \\), and the segment of v through x = 5 has slope \\( v'(5) = -3 \\).",
         "rule_named": "read the inner value and slope"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The outer slope is read at the inner output x = 3, not at x = 5: the segment of u there has slope \\( u'(3) = - \\frac{3}{2} \\).",
         "rule_named": "read the outer slope at the inner output"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "So \\( h'(5) = \\left(- \\frac{3}{2}\\right) \\cdot \\left(-3\\right) = \\frac{9}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            9,
            2
         ],
         "rule_named": "chain rule"
      }
   ],
